  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Heads-up and keep-warm",
      "items": [
        "The heads-up stays silent while a ping will keep the cache warm: this process's own ping is planned or out (willPing), or, in a process that does not hold the session lock, the lock holder's window file says willPing is true.",
        "A passive session warns unless the holder will ping. If the holder has stopped, or has nothing planned, this process's heads-up is the only warning.",
        "The holder writes willPing into the shared window file whenever its plan changes. The check runs when the heads-up is scheduled and again when its timer fires."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "VS Code, measured 11-12 Oct 2026",
      "items": [
        "The extension loads in VS Code's Copilot chat only with the setting \"chat.canvases.enabled\": true, from a project install (.github/extensions).",
        "Typed in full, /cache-clock works but is not listed in the / menu. Its card, help and settings appear as a question with an OK button, because plain session messages show there only as error boxes.",
        "The heads-up reaches only VS Code's log. Cold-send warnings are sent at error level there (the chat shows only error-level messages, as a failure box). Sessions keep usage checkpoints only, so the report counts them as totals."
      ]
    }
  ]
